/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A photon of wavelength λ carries energy E = hν = hc/λ.
   - An optical power of P watts is a stream of photons.
   - η = (electrons collected per second) ÷ (photons arriving per second)
   - η is a pure ratio with no units, between 0 and 1.
   - Photons are lost in three ways.
   - A photon is absorbed only if its energy is at least the bandgap Eg.
   - This is why silicon cannot be used in the 1.3 µm and 1.55 µm fiber windows: its cutoff is 1.11 µm.
   - Each collected electron carries charge q = 1.602 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.
   - Ip is the photocurrent in A and P the optical power falling on the diode in W.
   - R is the responsivity in A/W.
*/
