/* book exam traps: Putting λ in metres into R = ηλ/1.24. The 1.24 shortcut needs λ in micrometres; with λ in metres use R = ηqλ/(hc). | Mixing up the units: η has no units, R is in A/W. "η = 0.8 A/W" loses the mark. | Saying no detector can ever show R above λ/1.24. The ceiling is for the primary current; an APD with gain M shows MR, which can be far above it. | Taking η = 1 by default. Surface reflection, light that passes through, and recombination all make η less than 1. | Using R = ηλ/1.24 past the cutoff wavelength. Beyond λc = 1.24/Eg the material does not absorb, so R = 0, not a larger value. */
